*Heading
Variable-angle-tow composite S8R panel: ply fibre angles given by two *Distributions
** 40 x 10 panel, 8 x 2 S8R elements, clamped at x = 0, one instance rotated 30 deg about z.
** The fibre angle follows a linear variable-angle-tow path, theta = 0 deg at the clamp to
** 70 deg at the tip (one value per element column, +5 deg on the second row).  Layup
** [+theta / -theta / +theta+90 / -theta / +theta]: plies 1, 2, 4, 5 name the orientations
** Ori-P (+theta) and Ori-M (-theta), each built on its own *Distribution, ply 3 gives
** 90 deg relative to the section orientation Ori-P.  ccx 2.23 ignores a distribution on
** a shell section, so abq2ccx splits it per direction; validate_with_ccx.py checks that
** every node moves exactly as in distribution_shell_plate_explicit.inp, the same panel
** with one orientation pair and one *Shell Section per element.
**
